# Mobile env template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Copy to `.env` — NOT `.env.local`. Expo loads these highest-priority first:
#   .env.<mode>.local  →  .env.local  →  .env.<mode>  →  .env
# (<mode> is NODE_ENV: `development` for `expo start`, `production` for builds
# and exports; `.env.local` is skipped entirely in `test` mode.)
#
# `.env.local` exists to override a *committed* `.env`. Nothing here is
# committed — the root .gitignore ignores every `.env*` at any depth — so with
# nothing shared to override, a second file buys only a precedence puzzle.
# One file. Use `.env`.
#
# Only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` vars reach the client bundle. Metro inlines them by
# literal text match at build time, so `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
# is substituted and `process.env[name]` is not — write names out in full.
# Anything behind the prefix ships to every device: never put a secret there.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE ONLY AFFECTS THE LOCAL METRO DEV SERVER.
#
# Real system env vars beat dotenv files, so EAS builds ignore it entirely
# (and it is gitignored, so it never uploads). Every key below must ALSO be
# set in eas.json under `build.preview.env` and `build.production.env`, or
# those builds ship pointing at nothing.
#
# The `development` and `development-simulator` profiles do NOT need them:
# both are developmentClient builds that load JS from Metro at runtime, and
# Metro reads this file. That is why those two profiles carry only
# EAS_BUILD_PROFILE.
#
# So: adding a new EXPO_PUBLIC_* key is a two-place edit — here, and in the
# preview + production blocks of eas.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local Supabase stack. Run `pnpm db:start`, then `pnpm db:status` to read the
# API URL and anon key off the running containers.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
